\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Asset Group Structure Options\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Option 1\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Feed Only Asset Group
\f1\b0 \
This replicated Smart Shopping. You are only running product feed with no assets. The only inventory your ads will show for are Shopping ads and Dynamic Product Remarketing ads.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Option 2\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Full Asset Group
\f1\b0 \
With all assets you are now giving Google the ability to show your ads on all of their ad inventory.\
This is what Google originally intended for PMax to do. The feed only Asset Group is a bit of a loop hole right now and I predict Google will put an end to it in the future.\
\uc0\u55357 \u56481  
\f0\b Pro Tip:
\f1\b0  If you are just starting out then start with a Feed only Asset Group. Once your get success with Feed only then test adding assets.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Asset Group Best Practices\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The goal of Asset Groups is to group related products or product categories and create the most relevant asset creative to match those products.\
Don\'92t throw in unrelated products into the same Asset Group. Having Men\'92s shaving products mixed in with Women\'92s hair coloring in the same Asset Group will be impossible to create relevant asset creative for that is relevant to both those audience types.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

